Several outside bins were overflowing with rubbish, which they assumed was to blame for the odour. The trio made their way up the driveway, noticing that several deliveries, including three newspapers and two cartons of milk, had been ignored. They ascended the stairs to the front door. An envelope was stuck against it with brown packing tape. Leaving it be, they knocked and called out for Kathleen, but there was no response. Kathleen suffered from a medical condition known as Cushing disease, which often caused her to feel tired and unwell. Her friends worried that she might have fallen severely ill or had some other health emergency and was unable to answer them. One of the women rushed to the rear of their house where they knew Kathleen kept a spare key.
外面的几个垃圾桶里塞满了垃圾，他们认为这就是臭味的来源。三人沿着车道走去，注意到几份快递，包括三份报纸和两盒牛奶，都没有人理会。他们走上楼梯来到前门。一个信封用棕色包装胶带粘在门上。他们没有动它，而是敲门并呼喊凯瑟琳，但没有任何回应。凯瑟琳患有一种被称为库欣氏病的疾病，这常使她感到疲倦和不适。她的朋友们担心她可能病得很重，或者发生了其他健康紧急情况，无法回应他们。其中一名妇女冲向他们知道凯瑟琳存放备用钥匙的房子后部。

