00:11:21.000 --> 00:12:16.000
Kathleen had been stabbed with a sharp-tipped knife 52 times throughout her upper body. Her abdomen, chest and head had all been struck, with her face brutalised in such a manner that left her features unrecognisable. Yet, the wounds themselves were shallow, with the deepest measuring roughly four centimetres. Investigators speculated that Kathleen's attacker had either been a woman or a physically weaker man. In fact, only one wound was farmed to have been fatal. The severing of Kathleen's carotid artery in her neck resulted in her bleeding to death. Had she received intervention prior to losing consciousness, she might have survived. Kathleen didn't keep any opioids on site, and none of the prescription medications or other veterinary supplies had been touched,
凯瑟琳的上半身被一把尖刀刺了52次。她的腹部、胸部和头部都受到了重创，脸部被摧毁得面目全非。然而，伤口本身很浅，最深处大约只有四厘米。调查人员推测，凯瑟琳的袭击者要么是一名女性，要么是一名体力较弱的男性。事实上，只有一处伤口被认为是致命的。凯瑟琳颈部颈动脉的切断导致她失血过多而死。如果她在失去知觉前得到干预，她本可能幸存下来。凯瑟琳现场没有存放任何阿片类药物，也没有任何处方药或其他兽医用品被触碰，

