ruling out the possibility that the murder was motivated by theft. The focus turned to Kathleen's upper-level residence, which was in such disarray that police initially thought it had been ransacked and was part of the crime scene. Kathleen's friends clarified that this was just how her house always looked. There were no signs of forced entry into that area of the home, and nothing had been stolen. Amongst the clutter on Kathleen's dining table was her daily planner. The last entry was made on Thursday, February 26. 1998, three days before her body was discovered. Kathleen had jotted down a 12.30pm veterinary appointment for client Matthew Thompson and his dog, Jazz.
排除了谋杀是出于盗窃动机的可能性。调查重点转向了凯瑟琳楼上的住所，那里乱七八糟，警察最初认为它被洗劫过，是犯罪现场的一部分。凯瑟琳的朋友澄清说，她的房子一直都是这个样子。该区域没有强行闯入的迹象，也没有任何东西被盗。在凯瑟琳餐桌上的杂物中，有她的日常计划表。最后一条记录是在1998年2月26日星期四，即她被发现尸体的前三天。凯瑟琳记下了一个下午12点30分的兽医预约，客户是马修·汤普森和他的狗“爵士”。

