00:31:54.000 --> 00:33:04.000
Not wanting to impede on Kathleen's work, Victor and Pauline immediately left. Based on the timing, investigators were certain this man was the John Wilson Kathleen had been expecting. The fact that he was holding the cat in his arms indicated that he was a local, as travelling a long distance with an unrestrained cat would have proven difficult. Detectives had door-knocked the local area on the lookout for owners of seal point Siamese cats, but it wasn't until they saw a photo of one such cat published in the Korea Mail newspaper that their intrigue peaked. The cat was featured alongside an article titled, A Cult Joins Hunt. It described how various clairvoyants were trying to identify Kathleen Marshall's killer through techniques such as automatic writing. One clairvoyant named in the article was Ruth Bennett, a reverend, organist and marriage celebrant for the Spiritualist Church in Windsor.
不想妨碍凯瑟琳的工作，维克多和宝琳立即离开了。根据时间，调查人员确信这个男人就是凯瑟琳一直在等的约翰·威尔逊。他把猫抱在怀里的事实表明他是当地人，因为带着一只不受约束的猫长途旅行会很困难。侦探们在当地挨家挨户寻找海豹重点色暹罗猫的主人，但直到他们看到《信使邮报》上刊登的一张此类猫的照片时，他们的好奇心才达到顶峰。这只猫出现在一篇题为“邪教加入搜捕”的文章旁边。文章描述了各种通灵者如何通过自动书写等技术试图识别凯瑟琳·马歇尔的凶手。文章中提到的其中一位通灵者是露丝·贝内特，她是温莎灵性教会的牧师、管风琴手和婚礼司仪。

29
00:33:04.000 --> 00:34:06.000
She was also a member of the Cat Protection Society. The Spiritualist Church was founded on the belief that spirits of the dead want to communicate with the living. It was a popular place amongst members of the Cat Protection Society, including Virginia Houston, who attended the church regularly to receive spiritual direction. In the Korea Mail article, reverend Ruth Bennett had offered her opinion on Kathleen's murder, saying she'd picked up indications that it was motivated by money or outstanding debts. A photo of Ruth was featured in the story. In it, she was holding one of her pet cats, a seal point Siamese. Although it was the breed of cat detectives had been searching for, Ruth could not have been John Wilson. Still, the investigative spotlight was now on the Spiritualist Church.
她也是猫保护协会的成员。灵性教会建立在死者灵魂想要与生者交流的信念之上。它是猫保护协会成员中的热门场所，包括弗吉尼亚·休斯顿，她经常去教堂接受精神指导。在《信使邮报》的文章中，露丝·贝内特牧师对凯瑟琳的谋杀案发表了看法，称她感觉到这是出于金钱或未偿债务的动机。露丝的照片出现在报道中。照片中，她抱着她的一只宠物猫，一只海豹重点色暹罗猫。虽然这是侦探们一直在寻找的猫品种，但露丝不可能是约翰·威尔逊。尽管如此，调查的聚光灯现在集中在灵性教会身上。

30
00:34:06.000 --> 00:34:59.000
Investigators collected DNA samples from men who worked with or were known to the institution. During one such visit, a detective bumped into a frail-looking, bespectacled man who walked with a hunch. He introduced himself as 49-year-old Andrew Fitzherbert, a professional palm reader who carried out readings at the church. Most significantly, he was the de facto partner of reverend Ruth Bennett. According to all accounts, Andrew was a mild-mannered pacifist, though slightly odd and eccentric. He had many friends and no history of violence or prior convictions. The detective told Andrew why he was there and asked if he'd be willing to provide a blood sample. When told it was voluntary, Andrew abruptly refused.
调查人员从与该机构一起工作或认识的男性那里收集了DNA样本。在一次访问中，一名侦探撞见了一个看起来虚弱、戴着眼镜、驼背的男人。他自我介绍说是49岁的安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特，一名在教堂进行解读的专业手相师。最重要的是，他是露丝·贝内特牧师的事实伴侣。据所有描述，安德鲁是一个温和的和平主义者，尽管有点古怪和离奇。他有很多朋友，没有暴力史或前科。侦探告诉安德鲁他为什么来这里，并询问他是否愿意提供血样。当被告知这是自愿的时，安德鲁断然拒绝了。

31
00:34:59.000 --> 00:36:14.000
As the only witnesses that had crossed paths with the mysterious John Wilson, Victor and Pauline Lachati were handed a photo lineup that featured nine men. The couple immediately recognized photo number nine as the man who had visited Kathleen's house with a seal point Siamese cat before her murder. They'd gotten a good glimpse of him when they drove out of Kathleen's driveway as they had to wait for him to move out of the way. The photo the couple pointed out was that of Andrew Fitzherbert. Narrowing their sights on Andrew, investigators learned that he and Ruth Bennett had met in 1990 at the Theosophical Society, an organization that promotes the idea that a deeper spiritual reality can be established through techniques such as meditation. Andrew dedicated his time to advancing his spiritual awareness and had learned to detach himself from material possessions, only earning what he needed to live comfortably. Through their shared spiritual beliefs, Andrew and Ruth grew close.
作为与神秘的约翰·威尔逊擦肩而过的唯一目击者，维克多和宝琳·拉查迪拿到了一份包含九名男性的照片阵容。这对夫妇立即认出九号照片就是谋杀前带着海豹重点色暹罗猫访问凯瑟琳家的男人。当他们开车离开凯瑟琳的车道时，他们清楚地看到了他，因为他们不得不等他让路。这对夫妇指出的照片是安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特的。调查人员将目光锁定在安德鲁身上，了解到他和露丝·贝内特于1990年在通神学会相识，这是一个提倡通过冥想等技术建立更深层精神现实的组织。安德鲁致力于提升自己的精神意识，并学会了摆脱物质占有，只赚取舒适生活所需的钱。通过共同的精神信仰，安德鲁和露丝变得亲密起来。

32
00:36:14.000 --> 00:37:39.000
They ran a tea shop together that also offered tarot readings. It was there the pair met Virginia Houston, who became a regular customer and frequented the shop almost weekly. In 1995, Andrew and Ruth began working at the Spiritualist Church in Windsor and the following year, Virginia urged them to join the Cat Protection Society of Queensland. Ruth's application was processed after the six-month waiting period. For reasons unknown, Andrews was not. Detectives visited Andrew Fitzherbert at his home and noted his physically weak demeanour suited the shallow stab wounds that were inflicted on Kathleen Marshall. When Andrew refused to accompany detectives to the station for an interview, they were forced to place him under arrest. In custody, Andrew said he'd never even met Kathleen Marshall and had no idea where she lived. He only knew who she was because Virginia Houston complained about her constantly. In lieu of a clear motive, investigators wondered if Andrew's rejection from the Cat Protection Society had prompted him to violently confront Kathleen.
他们一起经营一家茶店，也提供塔罗牌解读。正是在那里，两人遇到了弗吉尼亚·休斯顿，她成了常客，几乎每周都光顾这家店。1995年，安德鲁和露丝开始在温莎的灵性教会工作，第二年，弗吉尼亚敦促他们加入昆士兰猫保护协会。露丝的申请在六个月的等待期后得到了处理。由于未知原因，安德鲁的申请没有。侦探们拜访了安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特，注意到他身体虚弱的举止与凯瑟琳·马歇尔身上造成的浅表刀伤相符。当安德鲁拒绝陪同侦探去警局接受采访时，他们被迫将他逮捕。在拘留期间，安德鲁说他甚至从未见过凯瑟琳·马歇尔，也不知道她住在哪里。他只知道她是谁，因为弗吉尼亚·休斯顿不断地抱怨她。在缺乏明确动机的情况下，调查人员怀疑安德鲁被猫保护协会拒绝是否促使他暴力对抗凯瑟琳。

33
00:37:39.000 --> 00:39:08.000
He vehemently denied this allegation, deeming it ridiculous, and those who knew both Kathleen and Andrew weren't aware that the pair had ever met. Andrew explained he wasn't John Wilson because he was doing palm readings from his office in Brisbane at the time John arrived for his 1pm appointment at Kathleen's clinic. Andrew's schedule for Thursday, February 26, which was filled out by his partner Ruth, featured the name Rose and a front at 1pm for an hour each. When asked to provide their contact details, Andrew couldn't. He claimed to only keep limited details about his clients because he didn't want to know any of their personal information prior to giving them a reading. Andrew and Ruth were provided a partial alibi by Ruth's ex-husband, who visited their home on the afternoon of Thursday, February 26. He remained there until 11pm when he said Andrew and Ruth went to bed. Kathleen could have been confronted as late as 3am, but Ruth maintained that Andrew was asleep the entire time. She questioned that if Kathleen had led Andrew into the clinic in the middle of the night, why was she found murdered in a blue and white sundress and not her pyjamas?
他极力否认这一指控，认为这很荒谬，而且那些既认识凯瑟琳又认识安德鲁的人都不知道他们两人曾经见过面。安德鲁解释说他不是约翰·威尔逊，因为在约翰于下午1点到达凯瑟琳诊所赴约时，他正在布里斯班的办公室里进行手相占卜。安德鲁2月26日星期四的日程表是由他的伴侣露丝填写的，上面写着“罗斯”和“前台”，每项各占一小时。当被要求提供客户联系方式时，安德鲁无法提供。他声称只保留有限的客户信息，因为他不想在给他们算命之前知道他们的任何个人信息。安德鲁和露丝得到了露丝前夫的部分不在场证明，他在2月26日星期四下午拜访了他们的家。他一直待到晚上11点，当时他说安德鲁和露丝上床睡觉了。凯瑟琳可能在凌晨3点才遭到袭击，但露丝坚称安德鲁一直都在睡觉。她质疑，如果凯瑟琳在半夜把安德鲁带进诊所，为什么她被发现遇害时穿着一件蓝白相间的夏日连衣裙，而不是睡衣？

34
00:39:08.000 --> 00:40:17.000
Although he continued to profess his innocence, Andrew still refused to provide a DNA sample. In the six hours he was held by police, he avoided going to the bathroom or drinking any water. Detectives applied for a court order that would allow them to forcibly obtain Andrew's blood, but their request was denied on the basis that there was insufficient evidence against him. However, they were granted a warrant to search his home. Three months had passed since Kathleen Marshall's murder when detectives approached Andrew Fitzherbert's residence with a search warrant in hand. They appealed to him one last time, calling him a reasonable man and insisting that all his troubles could be solved in a matter of seconds if he just gave them a blood sample. Andrew remained defiant. He was then asked if he had ever spoken with Kathleen Marshall on the telephone. Andrew answered no. The detective made a surprise revelation.
尽管他继续声称自己无罪，但安德鲁仍然拒绝提供DNA样本。在被警方拘留的六个小时里，他避免上厕所或喝任何水。侦探们申请了法院命令，允许他们强制获取安德鲁的血液，但他们的请求被驳回，理由是针对他的证据不足。然而，他们获得了搜查他家的搜查令。凯瑟琳·马歇尔遇害三个月后，侦探们拿着搜查令来到安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特的住所。他们最后一次向他呼吁，称他是一个讲道理的人，并坚持说如果他只是提供一份血液样本，他所有的麻烦都可以在几秒钟内解决。安德鲁仍然不为所动。随后，他被问及是否曾与凯瑟琳·马歇尔通过电话。安德鲁回答没有。侦探随后透露了一个令人惊讶的消息。

35
00:40:17.000 --> 00:41:43.000
Phone records had shown that a 64 second call placed to Kathleen's house on the Tuesday before she was killed had originated from Andrew's residence. The following day, four calls had been made to Kathleen's house from the spiritualist church at a time when Andrew was the only person present. Detectives believed Andrew had made these calls to stage a veterinary appointment with Kathleen using the fake name John Wilson. Although Kathleen only offered her veterinary services to friends and acquaintances, her phone number was readily available as she listed it in the courier mail newspaper each week when advertising her lapicua social dinner group. Andrew Fitzherbert turned pale and started to tremble, but he maintained that he'd never called Kathleen. He then changed his mind, conceding that he had called her to check on his application to the Cat Protection Society. Detectives carried out their search warrant specifically on the lookout for anything that could be used to obtain Andrew Fitzherbert's DNA. They confiscated his toothbrush, hairbrush, pillowcase, coffee mug and a handkerchief, all the while being screamed at by a visibly angry Ruth Bennett.
电话记录显示，在凯瑟琳遇害前的周二，打往她家的一通64秒的电话源自安德鲁的住所。第二天，在安德鲁是唯一在场的人时，从灵学会打出了四通电话到凯瑟琳家。侦探们认为安德鲁打这些电话是为了用假名“约翰·威尔逊”与凯瑟琳预约兽医服务。虽然凯瑟琳只向朋友和熟人提供兽医服务，但她的电话号码很容易获得，因为她每周在《信使邮报》上为她的拉皮库阿社交晚宴小组做广告时都会列出该号码。安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特脸色苍白，开始颤抖，但他坚持说他从未给凯瑟琳打过电话。随后他改变了主意，承认他确实给她打过电话，是为了查询他向猫咪保护协会提交的申请。侦探们执行了搜查令，专门寻找任何可以用来获取安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特DNA的东西。他们没收了他的牙刷、发刷、枕套、咖啡杯和手帕，在此过程中，露丝·贝内特一直愤怒地尖叫。

36
00:41:43.000 --> 00:42:53.000
Testing of Andrew's DNA samples were fast tracked, allowing the results to come back the next day. Samples taken from his handkerchief and one of his socks were compared with the profile of the male DNA found inside Kathleen's clinic. It was a match. Andrew Fitzherbert was placed under arrest and investigators were finally allowed to obtain a sample of his blood. It reinforced previous findings that it was his DNA in Kathleen's clinic. Investigators concluded that Andrew had likely injured himself during the attack, causing his blood to drop throughout the scene. He attempted to clean it up afterwards, but during this process, a few droplets of water down blood had splashed out from the sink and onto a nearby plastic bag. He then bled onto the cardboard box used to prop himself up and out of the window.
安德鲁的DNA样本检测被快速处理，结果在第二天就出来了。从他的手帕和一只袜子上提取的样本与在凯瑟琳诊所内发现的男性DNA图谱进行了比对。结果吻合。安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特被捕，调查人员终于获准获取了他的血液样本。这加强了之前的发现，即凯瑟琳诊所里的DNA确实是他的。调查人员得出结论，安德鲁在袭击过程中可能受了伤，导致他的血滴落在整个现场。他事后试图清理，但在清理过程中，几滴带血的水从水槽溅到了附近的塑料袋上。随后，他流血滴在了用来支撑他爬出窗户的纸板箱上。

37
00:42:53.000 --> 00:43:57.000
While police ran with this theory, Andrew refused to offer any explanation as to how his blood wound up in Kathleen's clinic. He stood by his story that he had never been there nor ever met her. He kept quiet and appeared unemotional as he was formally charged with Kathleen's murder. His partner Ruth Bennett also chose to remain silent. Andrew pleaded not guilty and faced the Brisbane Supreme Court in July 1999. In the absence of any witnesses, murder weapon or clear motive, the presence of Andrew Fitzherbert's DNA at the scene of the crime was fundamental to the prosecution's case. They argued that the DNA alone was enough to implicate him as the killer. As such, they didn't feel the need to address the Cat Protection Society and its internal conflicts or the mysterious circumstances surrounding John Wilson.
当警方根据这一理论进行调查时，安德鲁拒绝就他的血是如何出现在凯瑟琳诊所的做出任何解释。他坚持自己的说法，即他从未去过那里，也从未见过她。在被正式指控谋杀凯瑟琳时，他保持沉默，表现得毫无情绪。他的伴侣露丝·贝内特也选择保持沉默。安德鲁拒不认罪，并于1999年7月在布里斯班最高法院受审。在没有目击者、凶器或明确动机的情况下，安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特的DNA出现在犯罪现场是检方案件的基础。他们辩称，仅凭DNA就足以证明他是凶手。因此，他们觉得没有必要去处理猫咪保护协会及其内部冲突，或者关于“约翰·威尔逊”的神秘情况。

38
00:43:57.000 --> 00:44:59.000
Of primary importance was the sample of Andrew's blood found on the plastic bag by the sink. It was the only sample that also contained Kathleen's blood. This combination could have only occurred if both were injured at the same time, ruling out the possibility that Andrew had bled there on another occasion. The prosecution asserted that the chances of the DNA at the crime scene matching someone other than Andrew Fitzherbert was one in 1400 million. The defense highlighted the lack of motive as a major flaw in the prosecution's case. He also pointed out that the excessive amount of blood at the crime scene meant the killer would have been soaked red, which would have surely attracted attention. The possibility that Andrew had fled in his car to avoid witnesses couldn't be proven as it was never forensically examined.
最重要的是在水槽旁的塑料袋上发现的安德鲁的血样。这是唯一一个同时也含有凯瑟琳血液的样本。这种组合只有在两人同时受伤的情况下才会发生，排除了安德鲁在其他时间在那里流血的可能性。检方断言，犯罪现场的DNA与安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特以外的人相符的几率为14亿分之一。辩方强调缺乏动机是检方案件的一个重大缺陷。他还指出，犯罪现场过量的血液意味着凶手会被染成红色，这肯定会引起注意。安德鲁是否开车逃离以避开目击者这一可能性无法得到证实，因为他的车从未经过法医检查。

39
00:44:59.000 --> 00:46:02.000
In his testimony, Andrew said he'd never attacked anybody in his entire life and was not responsible for Kathleen's murder. He maintained he had no explanation for how his blood came to be in Kathleen's veterinary clinic. The prosecution emphasised that this mystery only seemed to implicate him further. They argued it would have been a smarter move if Andrew had just admitted to being in the clinic and had come up with an explanation from there, instead of avoiding the indisputable evidence. It took the jury four and a half hours to reach a verdict. For the murder of Kathleen Marshall, Andrew Fitzherbert was found guilty. It was the first time in Australia and only the third in the world that someone had been convicted of a crime based solely on DNA evidence. Andrew was visibly devastated.
在证词中，安德鲁说他一生中从未攻击过任何人，对凯瑟琳的谋杀案不负责任。他坚持说，对于他的血是如何出现在凯瑟琳的兽医诊所的，他没有任何解释。检方强调，这个谜团似乎只会让他更加难以脱身。他们辩称，如果安德鲁只是承认去过诊所并从那里编造一个解释，而不是回避无可辩驳的证据，那会是更明智的做法。陪审团花了四个半小时才达成裁决。因谋杀凯瑟琳·马歇尔，安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特被判有罪。这是澳大利亚历史上第一次、也是世界上第三次仅凭DNA证据就将某人定罪。安德鲁显然深受打击。

40
00:46:02.000 --> 00:46:44.000
A victim impact statement from Kathleen's siblings was presented to the court. It read, in part, Kathleen was estranged from us for some years. After the death of our parents, we went our separate ways. However, we never wished her any harm or unhappiness. In fact, we prayed that she would in fact achieve a very happy and harmonious life. Although Kathleen seemed to have been a difficult woman, she had also championed great causes. And like any person, she deserved to have lived a full and rich life free from criminal violence.
凯瑟琳的兄弟姐妹向法庭提交了一份受害者影响陈述。其中部分内容写道：凯瑟琳与我们疏远多年。父母去世后，我们各奔东西。然而，我们从未希望她受到任何伤害或不幸。事实上，我们祈祷她能过上非常幸福和谐的生活。虽然凯瑟琳似乎是一个难以相处的人，但她也支持过伟大的事业。像任何人一样，她理应过上充实而丰富的生活，远离犯罪暴力。

41
00:46:44.000 --> 00:47:43.000
Her murder was savage and brutal, and the person responsible deserved a hefty punishment. During sentencing, the judge told Andrew Fitzherbert, This is a crime of which you would not have been convicted, but for the recent explosion in knowledge in the field of genetics. He added that the motive would remain unknown unless Andrew chose to reveal it. Throughout the trial, Andrew had shown no remorse, and he would, quote, Now suffer the consequences of a conviction, if not your conscience, for what you have done. Andrew Fitzherbert was sentenced to life imprisonment, which in Queensland carried a minimum term of 15 years. Kathleen's friends and fellow members of the Cat Protection Society spoke of their relief that justice had been served,
她的谋杀案残忍而野蛮，肇事者理应受到严厉的惩罚。在宣判时，法官对安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特说：“这是一起如果没有遗传学领域知识的近期爆炸式增长，你本不会被定罪的犯罪。”他补充说，除非安德鲁选择揭露，否则动机将永远是个谜。在整个审判过程中，安德鲁没有表现出任何悔意，他将“现在承受定罪的后果，如果不是良心上的谴责，也是为你所做的一切承担后果”。安德鲁·菲茨赫伯特被判处终身监禁，在昆士兰州，这意味着至少15年的刑期。凯瑟琳的朋友和猫咪保护协会的成员们表示，他们对正义得到伸张感到宽慰，

42
00:47:43.000 --> 00:48:48.000
but the wider reaction to Andrew's guilty verdict was mixed. Some believed that his blood at the crime scene made it an open and shut case. Others weren't so sure, arguing that DNA evidence alone wasn't enough to convict. One of Andrew's supporters expressed disbelief that his mild-mannered and gentle friend could be ruled a violent killer, saying, It would be laughable if it wasn't so serious. The question was raised as to why Andrew was so reluctant to voluntarily provide a blood sample if he was innocent. Andrew maintained this was simply because he didn't trust the police. According to entomologist Professor Russell Luke, Kathleen Marshall was murdered sometime between Thursday, February 26 at 9pm and 3am Friday, February 27.
